=== TITLE: USG Abdomen & Pelvis (Pediatric / Child) ===
=== IMPRESSION ===
NORMAL SONOLOGICAL EVALUATION OF ABDOMEN AND PELVIS FOR AGE.
- No intussusception, appendicitis, or mesenteric lymphadenitis.

=== FINDINGS ===
STUDY: ULTRASONOGRAPHY OF ABDOMEN & PELVIS (PEDIATRIC)

FINDINGS:
- LIVER: Normal in size and shape according to pediatric age. Echotexture is homogeneous. No focal lesion or IHBRD seen.
- GALL BLADDER & BILIARY TRACT: Gall bladder is distended, lumen clear, wall thickness normal. CBD is normal in caliber.
- SPLEEN: Normal in size with homogeneous echotexture.
- PANCREAS: Visualized portions appear normal.
- KIDNEYS: Bilateral kidneys are normal in size, shape, and position. Normal corticomedullary differentiation. No calculus or hydronephrosis.
- URINARY BLADDER: Distended, normal wall thickness, lumen clear.
- BOWEL LOOPS & MESENTERY: Normal bowel peristalsis and wall thickness. No target sign, pseudokidney appearance (intussusception), or inflamed non-compressible blind-ended loop (appendicitis). No significant mesenteric lymphadenopathy.
- PERITONEAL CAVITY: No free fluid / ascites.